(7181694, 1102568, 19959, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>This shot meets the challenge and is technically well executed.<br/> <br/>The lighting is a little un-interesting though and does not help give this a WOW<br/>factor that would lift it in the voting.<br/> <br/>You might like to re-visit the subject and try some alternative takes on composition<br/>and lighting to see how a single subject can be made to look very different depending<br/>on treatment and approach.<br/> <br/>For example:<br/> <br/>Try daylight on one side with a reflector (or white sheet of paper) opposite to fill in the shadows<br/>Try a shallower depth of field to focus on the face and throw the body out of focus<br/> <br/>You''d be surprised at the learning curve of shooting around a subject and trying to get different<br/>looks...<br/> <br/>I look forward to seeing more of your photos on future challenges.<br/> <br/>Chris<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club This shot meets the challenge and is technically well executed. The lighting is a little un-interesting though and does not help give this a WOWfactor that would lift it in the voting. You might like to re-visit the subject and try some alternative takes on compositionand lighting to see how a single subject can be made to look very different dependingon treatment and approach. For example: Try daylight on one side with a reflector (or white sheet of paper) opposite to fill in the shadowsTry a shallower depth of field to focus on the face and throw the body out of focus You''d be surprised at the learning curve of shooting around a subject and trying to get differentlooks... I look forward to seeing more of your photos on future challenges. Chris ', '2014-02-26 08:32:08.000000', NULL, 0),
