(7182159, 1103072, 74979, '<td valign="top">prayers for your friend, Lydia.. and just as an anecdote of hope... when my friend Peter was dying this past fall, he was visited by friends of his, the wife of the couple had been diagnosed about 5 years ago w stage 4 breast ca w lytic bone mets.. prognosis <i>grim</i>.  She is currently still alive and well, and the lesions have healed.  So, not sure if this is science, miracle or a bit of both, but <b>there is hope</b>.<br/> <br/>Sadly, my friend Peter didnt make it.. he died very quickly after diagnosis, of a different kind of cancer.  <br/>I hope your friend, however long she has on this earth is able to make the most of her time, however she chooses.  <br/>XOXOXOXO<br/> <br/>Anni<br/> <br/>oh, I forgot to add.. nicely done taking 3rd place!!  congrats!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2014-02-27 11:55:53.</i></td>', 'prayers for your friend, Lydia.. and just as an anecdote of hope... when my friend Peter was dying this past fall, he was visited by friends of his, the wife of the couple had been diagnosed about 5 years ago w stage 4 breast ca w lytic bone mets.. prognosis grim.  She is currently still alive and well, and the lesions have healed.  So, not sure if this is science, miracle or a bit of both, but there is hope. Sadly, my friend Peter didnt make it.. he died very quickly after diagnosis, of a different kind of cancer.  I hope your friend, however long she has on this earth is able to make the most of her time, however she chooses.  XOXOXOXO Anni oh, I forgot to add.. nicely done taking 3rd place!!  congrats!', '2014-02-27 11:55:06.000000', '2014-02-27 11:55:53.000000', 0),
